Licensing status and scope
==========================

This repository combines work from several sources and is not distributed
under one project-wide license. The applicable terms depend on the file and
provenance described below and in NOTICE.md.

1. PipeNetwork inherited code
-----------------------------

Code inherited from PipeNetwork/kimi-k3-mlx, including later changes merged
from that repository, remains copyright its respective authors. As of upstream
commit 20a4fb101ce81380ab8af0036743d49e7256c521, that repository does not contain
an explicit top-level software license. This repository does not grant rights
to that inherited code. Obtain permission from its copyright holder unless an
applicable license is provided upstream.

2. Moonshot Kimi-K3 material
----------------------------

Kimi-K3 model weights, converted weights, configuration, and Moonshot-derived
reference code are governed by the Kimi K3 License in:

    LICENSES/Kimi-K3.txt

The license includes conditions for certain commercial Model-as-a-Service uses
and large commercial products. Read it before use or redistribution.

3. Apple MLX-LM-derived material
--------------------------------

Files retaining an Apple copyright notice, including the MLX-LM-derived UVMAX
loader and tool parser identified in NOTICE.md, are governed by Apple's MIT
License in:

    LICENSES/MLX-LM-MIT.txt

4. Original fork additions
--------------------------

Copyright (c) 2026 Michal Komar and contributors

Original, separable code, tests, benchmark tooling, and documentation first
authored in michalkomar/kimi-k3-mlx-distributed are offered under the MIT
License in:

    LICENSES/Fork-Additions-MIT.txt

This grant applies only to copyright held by those contributors. It does not
relicense inherited code, model weights, modifications inseparable from an
upstream work, or third-party material. When a file contains retained copyright
or license headers, those notices control that material.

See NOTICE.md for exact origins, commits, and attribution.
